than open language gaps. The installed v0.6.23 identifier fix closes that former Web gap without
weakening ambient-authority denial. Inventory count, lexical classification, a
single-file probe or a representative pilot cannot establish semantic parity
for an unclassified dependency graph.

The regenerated current project-graph queue contains 461 candidate paths and
249 unique graph contents. Only three are closed-and-direct probe-ready; 39
contain non-direct migration work and 419 have external or missing
dependencies. Thus the measurable open disposition queue is 9,489 unique
content clusters after subtracting the 75 security clusters and the newly
