Broad migration is complete only when G1 through G4 are all green, every
baseline path is migrated or explicitly retained with a cross-platform
disposition, reference/Web/Wasm conformance agrees, `.cljk` selects the same
qualified target semantics, and installed
release behavior evidence is archived. Until then `.kotoba` is usable for the
qualified subset, not a blanket `.cljc` replacement.

## Consequences

The safety model composes across a graph of same-language components instead
of treating all effects as opaque CLJC host code. The trusted base becomes
smaller but does not disappear. Existing pure pilots remain valid as
zero-import components; future pilots may exercise explicit provider imports
without opening ambient authority or production cutover.
